Patch summary:
Decode ASTC textures on the CPU on Mesa's Dozen (WSL2). gfxstream's GPU ASTC
decoder, compute shaders run through Dozen's D3D12 translation, is the main
suspect in GPU hangs there: Windows reset the GPU, D3D12 removed the device,
and gfxstream aborted on VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST, ending the VM (Asphalt 8 and 9
on a Radeon 780M).

- Build the CPU decoder: the Bazel build compiled the no-op one. A Bazel
  target for the bundled astc-encoder, decoder only: for AVX2, F16C, POPCNT
  and SSE4.1 on x86-64, which WSL2's Dozen hosts have, and NEON on ARM64.
  Before calling into it, gfxstream checks the CPU with
  __builtin_cpu_supports, which also checks that the OS saves AVX state (it
  read the AVX2 CPUID bit alone); without them it decodes on the GPU. On
  ARM64, where the check always failed, NEON now passes. Eight worker
  threads.
- VkEmulation picks CPU decoding when the device's driver is Dozen
  (VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_DOZEN), GPU decoding otherwise. IKA_ASTC_DECODE=cpu or
  gpu overrides it on any device.
- The CPU path decodes every region of a buffer-to-image copy: any number of
  copies per image, padded rows (bufferRowLength), layer pitch
  (bufferImageHeight), array layers and partial, block-aligned regions, with
  overflow-checked bounds on the guest's offsets. It used to decode one full,
  packed mip level per image and skip the rest, leaving them blank.
- The decoded texels' staging buffer belongs to the command buffer that
  copies from it, and goes when the command buffer is reset or freed; it used
  to stay for the image's lifetime, several times the size of its texture.
- An image whose ASTC data arrives some way the CPU cannot decode (an
  image-to-image copy, a source buffer the host has not mapped) is decoded on
  the GPU, from its compressed mipmaps, the next time it becomes readable,
  with a warning in the log.
- OpenGL ES offers GL_KHR_texture_compression_astc_ldr wherever the CPU
  decoder is available, as upstream intends, and its translator decodes
  ASTC uploads on the CPU. The no-op decoder kept ASTC out of the gfxstream
  mode on every host whose GL has no ASTC: Asphalt 8, whose textures are
  ASTC only, fell back to placeholders and drew its 3D world black.
- Unit tests of the CPU path's regions, bounds and staging buffers, with a
  fake driver and decoder, and of decoding with astc-encoder.
